% M7-T22 / D-0086 (c): A SOLVER CRASH on a legal four-variable model, exit 2,
% `Alldiff: d_fwd has no constraint id` -- found while reducing the bench/fuzz sweep's
% `Alldiff: ladder rung has no constraint id` crash, which is the same defect's other face
% (alldiff_overshoot_decl_top_unsat). FIXED; an ordinary passing model test whose proof is
% verified on every run.
%
% THE DEFECT. Four variables over three values: stage 1's pigeonhole arm pushes the
% surplus CONTAINED variable past the Hall interval [1, 3], and the push's telescope ran
% over [lo(y) .. b] whatever y's declared domain was. y here is d, declared 1..2, so the
% telescope asked for the forward channelling clause of d = 3, which does not exist.
%
% THE FIX is alldiff.ml's [prune_summands]: the telescope stops at decl_hi(y), where its
% residue is the constant false. Break: the pre-fix binary (sha256 a57f2961...) exits 2.
var 1..3: a :: output_var;
var 1..3: b :: output_var;
var 1..3: c :: output_var;
var 1..2: d :: output_var;
constraint all_different_int([a,b,c,d]);
solve satisfy;
